                <pb facs="0692" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.711/1902</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-28T19:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1894. My despatch No. 5177, February 16, transmitting French Government’s answer
                    to representations made regarding the forwarding of shipping documents.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d731-f1"/> Foreign Office in its note expresses willingness to
                    expedite without delay the dispatch of pouches marked “Shipping Documents” if
                    the Embassy will give assurance that the United States Government will assure
                    itself that such pouches intended for other than Allied countries only contain
                    bills of lading, consular invoices, or other shipping documents. Does Department
                    authorize me to reply that this proposal is acceptable?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
